ebtables-legacy-save runs "@sbindir@/ebtables" to list the rules; on this tree
that name is iptables' ebtables-nft (nftables backend), so the legacy save
script would dump the nft rule set instead of the legacy one. Run
ebtables-legacy, as the script's own name says. Written for FenrirOS.

--- a/ebtables-save.in
+++ b/ebtables-save.in
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 
 use strict;
 my $table;
-my $ebtables = "@sbindir@/ebtables";
+my $ebtables = "@sbindir@/ebtables-legacy";
 my $cnt = "";
 my $version = "1.0";
 my $table_name;
